{"decision":"REVISE","detail":{"days":14,"checkpoint":"You can write and run a small Python program that reads a CSV file, validates and groups the records, and prints a formatted summary report — with at least one function and one error-handling path."},"plans":[{"planRef":"plan_1","blueprint":{"schemaVersion":2,"strategy":{"policy":"ROADMAP","outcome":"Learn enough Python to build reliable small data-processing programs, starting from beginner level.","explanation":"Beginner with no observed history, so the first checkpoint is deliberately small: get a working environment and enough core syntax to write, run and debug a tiny program. That single integrated activity both teaches and checks readiness, so no separate diagnostic or practice set is booked. Later strategic scope (collections, functions, files, CSV/JSON, validation, aggregation, testing, packaging, and the small data-processing project) is retained as forecast phases with honest uncertainty; it is not booked now because the next useful checkpoint is only the first runnable program. No deadline exists, so the horizon is long and expansion should wait for fresh evidence.","recommendedEffort":{"lowMinutes":90,"likelyMinutes":150,"highMinutes":240},"phases":[{"localId":"phase_foundations","title":"Core syntax and first runnable program","outcome":"Write, run and debug a small Python program using variables, numeric and string types, conditionals and a loop.","effort":{"lowMinutes":90,"likelyMinutes":150,"highMinutes":240},"readinessCriterion":"A working script that takes input, branches on a condition, loops, and prints a formatted result."},{"localId":"phase_collections","title":"Collections and data structures","outcome":"Use lists, tuples, dictionaries, sets and nested collections to store and transform small datasets.","effort":{"lowMinutes":180,"likelyMinutes":300,"highMinutes":480}},{"localId":"phase_functions","title":"Functions and scope","outcome":"Decompose a program into functions with clear parameters, return values and local scope.","effort":{"lowMinutes":150,"likelyMinutes":240,"highMinutes":360}},{"localId":"phase_files","title":"Files, encodings and formats","outcome":"Read and write text files and parse CSV and JSON data with correct encoding handling.","effort":{"lowMinutes":180,"likelyMinutes":300,"highMinutes":480}},{"localId":"phase_data_processing","title":"Validation, aggregation and reporting","outcome":"Validate input records, group and aggregate them, sort results and produce a readable output report.","effort":{"lowMinutes":240,"likelyMinutes":420,"highMinutes":660}},{"localId":"phase_reliability","title":"Testing, debugging and error handling","outcome":"Test simple functions, handle boundary cases, log errors and debug programs systematically.","effort":{"lowMinutes":180,"likelyMinutes":300,"highMinutes":480}},{"localId":"phase_project","title":"Small data-processing project","outcome":"Build a small end-to-end data-processing program with modules, command-line arguments and a reusable transformation pipeline.","effort":{"lowMinutes":300,"likelyMinutes":540,"highMinutes":900}}]},"scope":[{"scopeRef":"scope_1","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Variables and expressions are the first building block for any runnable program."},{"scopeRef":"scope_2","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Numeric types support counting and aggregation in data processing."},{"scopeRef":"scope_3","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Strings are the primary input and output format for text data."},{"scopeRef":"scope_4","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"String formatting produces readable output reports."},{"scopeRef":"scope_5","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Boolean expressions drive validation and branching logic."},{"scopeRef":"scope_6","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Conditional branches let programs handle different data cases."},{"scopeRef":"scope_7","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"While loops support repeated processing until a condition is met."},{"scopeRef":"scope_8","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"For loops iterate over records and collections, central to data processing."},{"scopeRef":"scope_9","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Lists hold ordered sequences of records or values."},{"scopeRef":"scope_10","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Slicing extracts subsets of sequences for targeted processing."},{"scopeRef":"scope_11","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Tuples represent fixed-shape records such as rows."},{"scopeRef":"scope_12","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Dictionaries map keys to values, enabling grouping and lookup."},{"scopeRef":"scope_13","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Sets support deduplication and membership checks."},{"scopeRef":"scope_14","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Nested collections model realistic structured data."},{"scopeRef":"scope_15","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Functions decompose programs into reusable units."},{"scopeRef":"scope_16","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Parameters and return values define function interfaces."},{"scopeRef":"scope_17","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Local scope prevents unintended state sharing between functions."},{"scopeRef":"scope_18","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Exceptions handle malformed or unexpected data gracefully."},{"scopeRef":"scope_19","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"File reading loads external data into programs."},{"scopeRef":"scope_20","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"File writing persists processed results."},{"scopeRef":"scope_21","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Text encodings ensure correct handling of non-ASCII data."},{"scopeRef":"scope_22","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"CSV parsing is the standard format for tabular data input."},{"scopeRef":"scope_23","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"JSON parsing handles structured data interchange."},{"scopeRef":"scope_24","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Data validation catches bad records before processing."},{"scopeRef":"scope_25","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Grouping and aggregation produce summary statistics."},{"scopeRef":"scope_26","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Sorting records makes reports readable and deterministic."},{"scopeRef":"scope_27","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Date parsing handles temporal fields in data."},{"scopeRef":"scope_28","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Modules organize code into reusable files."},{"scopeRef":"scope_29","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Package environments manage dependencies reproducibly."},{"scopeRef":"scope_30","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Testing simple functions catches errors early."},{"scopeRef":"scope_31","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Boundary cases reveal edge conditions in data processing."},{"scopeRef":"scope_32","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Logging errors aids debugging and monitoring."},{"scopeRef":"scope_33","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Command-line arguments make programs configurable."},{"scopeRef":"scope_34","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Program decomposition keeps code maintainable."},{"scopeRef":"scope_35","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Readable names improve code clarity."},{"scopeRef":"scope_36","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Basic debugging skills resolve runtime errors."},{"scopeRef":"scope_37","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Reusable transformations avoid duplicated logic."},{"scopeRef":"scope_38","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Input contracts define expected data shapes."},{"scopeRef":"scope_39","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"Output reports present results to users."},{"scopeRef":"scope_40","disposition":"INCLUDED","contribution":"The small data-processing project integrates all prior skills into a complete program."}],"activities":[{"localId":"first_program","outcomeRefs":["phase_foundations"],"scopeRefs":["scope_1","scope_2","scope_3","scope_4","scope_5","scope_6","scope_7","scope_8","scope_36"],"title":"Write and run your first small Python program","activityType":"Integrated learning and check","purpose":"Establish a working environment and confirm you can write, run and debug a small program using variables, conditionals and a loop.","instructions":"1. Install Python 3 and confirm it runs by opening a terminal and typing `python3 --version`.
2. Create a file named `first_program.py`.
3. In it, write a program that:
   - stores a name in a variable and prints a greeting using an f-string;
   - asks the user for a number with `input()`, converts it to an integer, and prints whether it is even or odd using an if/else;
   - uses a for loop to print the numbers 1 through that number, one per line.
4. Run the program with `python3 first_program.py` and try at least three different inputs, including 0 and a negative number.
5. If you get an error, read the traceback, fix the line it points to, and run again. Write down in one sentence what the error was and how you fixed it.
6. When it runs correctly for all three inputs, you are done.","completionCriterion":"The program runs without errors for three different inputs (including 0 and a negative number) and produces the expected greeting, even/odd message and number list each time.","effort":{"lowMinutes":45,"likelyMinutes":75,"highMinutes":120},"timeboxMinutes":60,"commitment":{"category":"COMMITTED"},"hardDependencies":[],"cognitiveDemand":"MODERATE","stoppingCondition":"Stop once the program runs correctly for all three inputs and you have noted one error-and-fix if any occurred."}]},"decisions":{"assumptions":["The learner has a computer with internet access to install Python.","No prior programming experience is assumed.","The learner can read English well enough to follow instructions."],"tradeOffs":["Booked only one integrated activity instead of separate lessons, practice sets and a diagnostic, because a single runnable program both teaches and checks the first checkpoint.","Deferred all later phases to forecast only, since no deadline exists and the next useful checkpoint is the first working program."],"unresolvedUncertainty":["Actual pace of learning core syntax is unknown; the first activity will reveal whether the estimate is realistic.","Whether the learner has any prior exposure to programming is unknown."],"stoppingConditions":["Stop the current plan when the first program runs correctly for three inputs; do not add extra exercises.","Do not start later phases until the first checkpoint is met and a fresh request is made."]}}],"sharedDependencies":[],"tradeOffExplanation":"Booked one integrated activity that both teaches and checks the first runnable program, instead of separate lessons, practice sets and a diagnostic; all later scope is retained as forecast phases because no deadline exists and the next useful checkpoint is small."}
